sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant UI as Client App
    participant API as  Server
    participant DB as  DB

    U->>UI: Enter server URL, username, password

    rect rgb(245,245,245)
    Note over UI,API: Registration Flow
    UI->>API: GET /get-parameters
    API-->>UI: 200 {P,G}
    UI->>UI: pass_x = derive(password)
    UI->>UI: secret_y = g^pass_x mod p
    UI->>API: POST /register {client_id, secret_y}
    API->>DB: Insert/update user(client_id, secret_y)
    DB-->>API: OK
    API-->>UI: 201 Created/200 Updated
    UI-->>U: Registration success/error
    end

    rect rgb(235,245,255)
    Note over UI,API: Login Flow
    UI->>API: GET /get-parameters
    API-->>UI: 200 {P,G}

    UI->>UI: password_x = derive(password)
    UI->>UI: Generate random r <br/> t = g^r mod p

    UI->>API: POST /login/commit {client_id, commitment_t=t}
    API->>DB: Validate user exists
    DB-->>API: User record
    API->>API: Compute binding = SHA-256(remote_addr|user_agent|session_id)
    API->>API: c = SHA-256(session_id|client_id|t|binding) mod (Q-1) + 1
    API->>API: Store commitment, challenge, binding in memory
    API-->>UI: 200 {challenge_c}

    UI->>UI: Compute s = (r + c*x) mod q
    UI->>API: POST /login/verify { solution_s=s } + X-Auth-Session header
    API->>API: Recompute binding from remote_addr, user_agent, session_id
    API->>API: Reject with 401 if binding mismatch (relay detected)
    API->>API: Recompute c from stored inputs — reject with 400 if mismatch
    API->>DB: Read user secret_y
    DB-->>API: secret_y
    API->>API: Verify g^s == t * y^c (mod p)
    alt Verification success
        API->>DB: Create/update AuthToken (JWT)
        DB-->>API: Token stored
        API-->>UI: 200 {token, client_id}
        UI-->>U: Show auth success + token
    else Verification failure
        API-->>UI: 401 {reason}
        UI-->>U: Show error
    end
    end

    rect rgb(245,255,245)
    Note over UI,API: Authenticated Data Flow
    UI->>API: GET/POST/PUT /data with Authorization token
    API->>API: Decode and validate JWT
    API->>DB: Read/write personal data
    DB-->>API: Data result
    API-->>UI: 200/201/error
    UI-->>U: Display result
    end

    Note over API: adds headers to every response
